  "note": "Per-architecture SM DRAM rate facts, regenerated by `tools/bench/warp_inflight/warp_inflight.py regenerate` from the committed probe runs in src/core/data/warp_inflight/ (one warp_inflight_<arch>.txt per architecture, written by `warp_inflight.py run` on one card of it; never edited by hand), read by core/sm_rate_facts.h for the decode price's per-SM bound min(P, W x b_w / L0) (kernel_roofline.h dram_time, #690). sm_dram_bytes_per_clock_free / _placed: P, the largest rate one SM reached at k = 1 (any variant, any W) over the SM clock of that row, with the L1-largest carve-out (`free`) and the shared-largest one (`placed`); sm_dram_gbps_* and sm_mhz_* are the rate and clock it was read from. dram_stream_latency_ns: L0, the run's own fetch time of one warp alone on one SM with one 16-byte streaming load a lane in flight (free, k = 1, chain1, W = 1): the loads the law prices, not the ISA table's pointer chase (dram_tlbwarm_latency_ns_w1, 8-24 % shorter on the same card). ring2_*: the decode kernels' two-slot ring with two loads a lane a slot (2048 B a warp in flight by count): b_w at W = 1 by Little's law on L0, and the largest W up to which every row keeps 0.9 of it; chain4_b_w_w1_free and ring4_b_w_w1_free the same for 4 loads a lane in one chain and for the 4-load ring (4096 B by count). ring2_rows: the ring2 rows at k = 1, [W, GB/s an SM], the measurement the law's check reads (tests/ops/linear/test_kernel_roofline.cpp). Provenance Measured for every row, with its source file, card, probe version, nvcc, driver, runtime and the sha256 of the warp_inflight.cu it was built from; a row of another card of the architecture than the board priced is a transfer within the architecture. tests/test_warp_inflight.py pins that the table equals its regeneration and that every committed run is of the checked-in probe.",
